{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 113, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With no node1->output edge, removing the direct input->output edge eliminates more of the remaining signal paths."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the strongest conv on the final edge with a parameter-free pool removes substantial learned capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a skip where edge 0 was empty reconnects node 1 and revives downstream paths through edges 2 and 4."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Creating a direct conv input->output path where none existed helps far more than swapping an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty edge into the output with a 3x3 conv adds a new parametric path, unlike replacing an existing conv."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading a parameter-free skip to a 3x3 conv adds capacity, while replacing a conv yields little change."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct input->output edge, the node-2 path carries more of the signal, so degrading it to pooling hurts more."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a 3x3 conv into the output loses capacity, whereas removing a skip or pool can be neutral or beneficial."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If node 2 has no input from node 1, removing edge 1 makes node 2 dead and also nullifies edge 5."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With node 1 disconnected, edge 3 carries most of the output, so turning it into a pool costs much more."}], "tok": 17580, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [1, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [2, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [2, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [1, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none"], [5, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [2, "skip